CLAIM 14 — Semgrep / SAST runs automatically after code-related goals

Scope of inspection (static only): src/goal/build-gate.ts,
src/goal/agent-executor.ts, src/config/types.goal.ts, src/goal/build-gate.test.ts,
src/goal/agent-executor.test.ts, .semgrepignore.

What the code actually does
============================

A. The Semgrep run is built into the build gate, not a separate post-run hook.
   It is automatic when the binary is on PATH; the operator can change cadence
   via config.

   - src/config/types.goal.ts:3 — `export type SemgrepMode = "off" | "step" | "goal";`
   - src/config/types.goal.ts:31-32 — `semgrep?: SemgrepMode` on the goal
     config (the operator toggle).
   - src/goal/build-gate.ts:7 — `const DEFAULT_SAST_SEMGREP_ENABLED = true;`
     (default ON).
   - src/goal/build-gate.ts:160-193 — `buildDefaultSastCommand({ workingDir,
     targetPaths })` shells `which semgrep`; if the binary is missing it
     returns `null` and SAST is silently skipped. Otherwise it returns:
     `semgrep scan --config auto --error --quiet --severity ERROR
       --timeout 600 --exclude 'node_modules' --exclude 'dist' --exclude '.git'
       --exclude '.next' --exclude 'build' --exclude '*.test.ts'
       --exclude '.moltbot-goal-worker-results' <target>`

B. Semgrep is composed with the project's existing build gate.

   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:179 — `const semgrepMode = config?.goal?.semgrep
     ?? "step";` (default cadence is per-step).
   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:539-555 — when `semgrepMode === "step"` and a
     task has just been reported done, the executor resolves the list of files
     changed since the per-task checkpoint, builds a path-scoped semgrep
     command via `buildDefaultSastCommand`, and prepends it to the existing
     `plan.buildGate.commands` before running them.
   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:565 — `runBuildGateCommands(commandsForThisStep,
     workingDir)` captures real exit codes; a non-zero exit puts the step into
     `blocked` (see claim-08 log).
   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:732-737 — when `semgrepMode === "goal"` and
     every step is done, the *final* build gate prepends one whole-repo
     semgrep scan.
   - src/goal/agent-executor.ts:579-588 — infrastructure-class failures
     (e.g. "Failed to resolve 'semgrep.dev'") are classified separately and
     route to a `build_gate_infra_failed` block instead of being treated as
     a code finding (see build-gate.ts:15-19).

C. Failure handling is opinionated and tested.

   - src/goal/build-gate.ts:220-228 — `makeBuildGateFailurePrompt` adds
     Semgrep-specific remediation guidance ("Suppress Semgrep findings at
     exact offending lines with explicit rule IDs (e.g. # nosemgrep: rule-id)
     ...") only when the failed command is a semgrep scan.
   - src/goal/agent-executor.test.ts:902, 970, 1004, 1046 — regression
     tests cover semgrep infra failures, `semgrep: "off"`, `semgrep: "step"`,
     and `semgrep: "goal"`.

D. The repo carries a checked-in `.semgrepignore` (file at repo root, observed
   via grep).

