Safe README wording
===================
- "Code-related runs automatically include a Semgrep static-analysis pass in
  the build gate. By default it runs after each step (cadence configurable
  to `off` / `step` / `goal`) and a failed scan blocks the step the same way
  any other build-gate command failure does."
- "If `semgrep` is not on the PATH, the SAST step is silently skipped — the
  rest of the build gate still runs."

Unsafe wording to avoid
=======================
- "Semgrep is run as a separate post-run security audit." (It is composed
  into the existing build gate, not a separate post-run audit.)
- "Semgrep findings always block the goal." (They block only when cadence
  is `step` / `goal` AND semgrep is on PATH AND the policy is `--error
  --severity ERROR`.)
- "Semgrep policy is locked." (Operator can override via
  `config.goal.semgrep` and via `.semgrepignore`.)

STATUS: verified
REASON: Default Semgrep cadence is `"step"` (agent-executor.ts:179) with
`DEFAULT_SAST_SEMGREP_ENABLED = true` (build-gate.ts:7); the executor
prepends a path-scoped semgrep scan to the build gate after each completed
step and a whole-repo scan to the final gate when configured. Failures
route through the normal blocked/build-gate path (see claim-08). Not
roadmap — implemented, tested, and on by default.
